    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "Hello, everyone. This week at Nurturing Wellbeing with Kurt Kelly, we turn and take a national approach. I have a great guest, one that is recognized probably all over the United States, maybe all over the world. He worked years with CNN as a commentator, and he was also a U.S. Senator, that Senator Rick Santorum. Rick is going to be talking about the Family Leave Act. I got to tell you, this is a real important topic as we look to nurture well-being. And I think you're really going to enjoy this episode. We're going to try to do more of these things as we bring in national speakers on national issues. But the introduction of this episode is another good friend and that's Liza McFadden. Liza is an expert in this arena in her own right. It's very active here in Florida. And so I think you're going to really enjoy conversation with Liza McFadden and then Senator Rick Santorum. There's a national movement that's taking place and it's called the Family Leave Act. It's giving children and families an opportunity to bond together and see the science that takes place there. This was introduced to me by a young lady that probably for many folks here in Florida doesn't need any introduction. yet she is well known for much of her work that she's done in the philanthropic world and compassion world. Liza McFadden, Liza has her own business now. It's called Liza and Partners. And she is the one that came to me and asked me if I wanted to get involved. And of course, you can't tell Liza, no, so, and I wasn't going to do anyhow. Why is it welcome? I just, I want you to introduce, before we bring Senator Santoram on, I want you to introduce the Family Leave Act concept and how Floridians can get involved.",
